safix::generator_definition_drifted

  × clan considers the generator 'ntfy' on ana-workstation outdated, so
  │ exporting
  │ the mapping 'ntfy-token' would write a value clan's next generation
  │ replaces.
  │ 
  │ clan records a validation for each generator and regenerates when the
  │ recorded one no longer matches the definition. That has already happened
  │ here, so the next routine
  │ 
  │     clan vars generate ana-workstation
  │ 
  │ would discard whatever this export wrote, without saying so.
  │ 
  │ Two ways out. Either bring clan's side back into agreement, by running
  │ that generation now and accepting the value it mints; or declare this
  │ mapping clan-to-safix instead, which is the right shape when clan's
  │ generator is what produces the value.
  │ 
  │ There is no option that exports anyway. safix has nowhere to record that
  │ this var is externally supplied, so proceeding would be a silent loss
  │ rather than an accepted risk.
